title: The Local Elections
tags: event
view-if: time = 5
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
go-to: good if con_lead >= 2; mixed if con_lead < 2 and con_lead > -2; bad if con_lead <= -2

= The Local Elections

The May local elections are the last big test of opinion before Callaghan has to choose a date.

@good
on-arrival: resources += 1; loyalist_dissent -= 4; wet_dissent -= 2; thatcher_rating += 1

We make solid gains in the London boroughs and the metropolitan districts. Volunteers return to the constituencies with their tails up.

@mixed
on-arrival: loyalist_dissent += 1

A mixed night. We hold our own, and Labour does better than the papers expected.

@bad
on-arrival: loyalist_dissent += 4; wet_dissent += 4; thatcher_rating -= 2

Labour recovers ground across the cities. The Sunday papers run profiles of Willie Whitelaw as a leader-in-waiting.
